From ab2e6fe4b4a8de9f93dd8b0e2d600beae4c4a90f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: frogro <frank.grootens@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:16:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH RFC 15/22] drm: apple: connect and retire M1 USB4 display
 routes from kernel events

Carry the DP121 DRM source used by DP125: explicit route type, provider lifetime, firmware callback handling, HPD withdrawal and automatic initial/reconnect lifecycle. The USB4 role bit is adapted from Oliver Lukschander commit e37bbb4fc8f577967ea3acd8b2c27e0ce91f1138 in omacom/linux-aurora; original metadata is packaged separately. Local macOS/m1n1 captures and DP105-125 tests inform the ordering. Keep diagnostic identifiers so source provenance remains reviewable; no direct Type-C DP-alt, MST, dock-unplug or suspend support is asserted.

Prepared with AI assistance from the recorded local experiments. No maintainer review or DCO sign-off is asserted.
